lantern-pr 1
# 25
#title feat: add local Diagnostics for Lantern's own errors and crashes
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/25
#branch feat/app-diagnostics
#base main
#opened 2026-11-10
#head 05e829bf3180da24f1c1a9ff67432b0940d6191c
#describe what Lantern keeps a local, bounded, redacted log of its own errors, crashes and editor-server problems, shows it live in a Diagnostics view and reads earlier runs after a restart.
#describe what The user can copy a redacted report or open a prefilled GitHub issue; Lantern makes no network call and sends nothing itself.
#describe before A misconfigured editor server on Windows ended in a blank editor and one line of text, and a crash left nothing behind.
#describe after The failure is an entry with the exit code, command, last output and a Windows hint, readable and copyable, with home folders, project folders and tokens removed.
#describe after After a crash the next start shows a one-time notice with Report on GitHub and Dismiss.
#describe verified Typecheck and lint pass; the unit suite passes except one licences test that needs packages missing from this worktree's shared node_modules.
#describe verified The view itself was not looked at, as the app cannot be opened from this run.
